{"text": "190246246\n\n2 \u2018Stoven Milloy <milloy@cais.net> on 01/05/2000 03:49:14 PM\n\nTo: milloy@cais.com\nce (bec: Sharon BoyseiLouisvillelJS/BAT)\nSubject: Upcoming studies of interest\n\nBritish American Tobacco - Special Security Notice\nMillennium Viruses - Beware Attachments\n\nViruses can cause enormous damage to our Information Technology which could even result\nin complete system shutdown and loss of business data. File attachments from external sources,\nare the main carriers of viruses.\n\nIn the period 1 - 19 December 1999, when itis assessed that risks of virus attachments will\nincrease, you are requested to delete attachments if in doubt of the trustworthiness of the source\n\nIn the period 20 December - 5 January when the risks are crtcal, al file attachments will be\nautomatically removed. For business critical communication use either email text or make\nalternative arrangements (e.g. fax)\n\nBeyond 6th January please follow same precautionary actions as period 1 - 19 December 1999\nnti all risks have been assessed and you are advised to revert back to normal operations.\n\nPlease bear with the inconvenience. Its in the interest of the Company.\n\nThe following studies will be in upcoming issues of the American Journal of\nEpidemiology. I'm tying to get advance copies.\n\nSteve\nJan. 15:\n131 Prospective Study of Hepatitis B and C Viral infections, Cigarette\n\u2018Smoking, Alcohol Consumption, and Other Factors Associated with\nHepatocellular Carcinoma Risk in Japan. Mitsuru Mori, Megumi Hara, tkuko\nWada, Toshiya Hara, Kyosuke Yamamoto, Morisada Honda, and Junichi Naramoto\n148 Health Problems in Teenage Daily Smokers versus Nonsmokers, Norway,\n\n1995-1997: The Nord-Trendelag Health Study. Turid Lingaas Holmen,\nElizabeth Barrett-Connor, Jostein Holmen, and Leif Bjermer\n\nFeb. 1\n\n241 Environmental Tobacco Smoke and Lung Cancer. A Case-Control Study in\nGermany, Michaela Kreuzer, Martin Krauss, Lothar Krelenbrock, Karl-Heinz_\n\nPRODUCED FROM B&W WEB SITE",
